<%- include('../partials/admin-top', { title }) %>

<h1>Review knowledge</h1>
<p class="sub">Knowledge grows by accretion — starter entries, suggestions approved over months, things written in a hurry. Nothing here is changed automatically; it's a list of what's worth a look. <a href="/admin/faqs">← back to Knowledge</a></p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="stat"><div class="num"><%= warnings.total %></div><div class="lbl">entries</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="num"><%= overlaps.length %></div><div class="lbl">overlapping pairs</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="num"><%= warnings.placeholders.length %></div><div class="lbl">unfinished</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="num"><%= warnings.unused.length %></div><div class="lbl">never used</div></div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Find and replace</h2>
  <p class="sub">Swap text across every entry and guide at once — a changed download code, a renamed app. Best used to convert a hardcoded code into a placeholder (<code>{purple}</code> or <code>{skyglass}</code>), so the next change is one field in <a href="/admin/bot">Bot settings</a> instead of this.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/admin/faqs/replace">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="find">Find</label>
        <input id="find" name="find" type="text" required value="<%= preview ? preview.find : '' %>" placeholder="9804805">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="replace">Replace with</label>
        <input id="replace" name="replace" type="text" value="<%= preview ? preview.replace : '' %>" placeholder="{purple}">
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">Exact text, case sensitive. Leave <em>Replace with</em> empty to delete the text.</p>
    <p><button class="btn-ghost" type="submit">Preview</button></p>
  </form>

  <% if (preview) { %>
  <div style="border-left:3px solid var(--warn);padding-left:12px;margin-top:16px">
    <p><strong><%= preview.total %></strong> item(s) contain “<%= preview.find %>”. Nothing has changed yet.</p>
    <% for (const f of preview.faqs) { %>
      <p class="hint">entry #<%= f.id %> — <%= f.question %></p>
    <% } %>
    <% for (const g of preview.guides) { %>
      <p class="hint">guide — <%= g.title %></p>
    <% } %>
    <form method="post" action="/admin/faqs/replace">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="find" value="<%= preview.find %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="replace" value="<%= preview.replace %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="apply" value="1">
      <button type="submit">Replace in all <%= preview.total %></button>
    </form>
  </div>
  <% } %>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Entries that say nearly the same thing</h2>
  <p class="sub">This is the expensive kind of mess: retrieval has to choose between two entries that each half-cover a question, and the keyword fallback just picks the higher score — which is how a narrow entry ends up answering a broad question word for word. Merge the pair into one fuller entry, or make each one clearly about its own thing.</p>
  <% if (overlapError) { %>
    <p class="hint">⚠️ Couldn't compare: <%= overlapError %></p>
  <% } else if (!overlaps.length) { %>
    <p class="hint">No overlapping pairs — either your entries are nicely distinct, or the embedding model isn't available to compare them (check <a href="/admin/ai">AI settings</a> → Test connection).</p>
  <% } else { %>
    <% for (const o of overlaps) { %>
    <div style="border-left:3px solid var(--warn);padding-left:12px;margin-bottom:18px">
      <p class="hint"><%= Math.round(o.score * 100) %>% alike</p>
      <p><a href="/admin/faqs?edit=<%= o.a.id %>"><strong><%= o.a.question %></strong></a> <span class="badge badge-dim">used <%= o.a.hit_count %>×</span></p>
      <p><a href="/admin/faqs?edit=<%= o.b.id %>"><strong><%= o.b.question %></strong></a> <span class="badge badge-dim">used <%= o.b.hit_count %>×</span></p>
    </div>
    <% } %>
  <% } %>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Unfinished</h2>
  <p class="sub">Drafted answers still carrying an <code>[ADMIN: …]</code> gap. The bot will read these out as they are.</p>
  <% if (!warnings.placeholders.length) { %><p class="hint">None. 🎉</p><% } %>
  <% for (const f of warnings.placeholders) { %>
  <p><a href="/admin/faqs?edit=<%= f.id %>"><%= f.question %></a><% if (!f.enabled) { %> <span class="badge badge-dim">disabled</span><% } %></p>
  <% } %>
</div>

<div class="row">
  <div class="card">
    <h2>Never used</h2>
    <p class="sub">Enabled, over a month old, never once matched. Could be dead weight — or a seasonal answer that's simply out of season. Your call.</p>
    <% if (!warnings.unused.length) { %><p class="hint">None.</p><% } %>
    <% for (const f of warnings.unused) { %>
    <p><a href="/admin/faqs?edit=<%= f.id %>"><%= f.question %></a></p>
    <% } %>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h2>No keywords</h2>
    <p class="sub">Fine while the AI is matching by meaning, but these are invisible to the keyword fallback — so they vanish exactly when the endpoint is down and you need them most.</p>
    <% if (!warnings.noKeywords.length) { %><p class="hint">None.</p><% } %>
    <% for (const f of warnings.noKeywords) { %>
    <p><a href="/admin/faqs?edit=<%= f.id %>"><%= f.question %></a></p>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/admin-bottom') %>
